into recorded decisions. Health's \"same status queries as `ep status`\" is an honest partial given the disclosed checkpoint gap — registration/discovery/indexing genuinely work, extraction/embedding degrade honestly rather than fabricate. Inbox's 50-item default cap survives the rewiring (`build-inbox`'s own default, workbench.clj's handlers pass no `:limit` override). Note for follow-up, not blocking: neither `path-revisions` (timeline) nor `query-status` (health) have an equivalent cap — a large corpus could walk unbounded commit history or stage lists in these two views. Worth a follow-up card; not severe enough to block given the existing disclosed-gap precedent this session has already set.\n\nNo new defects found. Recommend a follow-up card for the checkpoint-schema/ingestion-run join (pre-existing, cross-cutting — also affects the already-done ENG-006A) and, optionally, timeline/health paging — not creating one per instructions, flagging for the board owner.", :source "agent", :agent "eta-mu", :write-id "1784688785485-0.8rrynk68itn58c06pk4", :type "comment"}, :causal/root "a9f1832c-dbd3-4de2-8b27-0d3e0cdbcbd9"}
